open_file_algorithm {
    When the editor opens or changes a `.rq` buffer, the language server must run this sequence.
    Do not wait for workspace Linked. Do not wait for a full SQLite crawl.
    Detail: [open_file_sequence_diagram].
    Related: [open_file_reference_sequencing], [ast_lifecycle], [outbound_one_hop],
    [open_file_hot_path], [token_colour_sequence], [missing_reference_colour_sequence],
    [lazy_features_after_outbound].

    1. Populate the Langium AST for this buffer only ([ast_lifecycle]).
       CST and AST exist at `DocumentState.Parsed`. Later builder phases do not rebuild the tree.
    2. Colour tokens in this buffer ([token_colour_sequence]).
    3. Identify outbound reference targets from native local extract plus this AST
       ([local_symbolic_analysis]).
    4. For each target that is another file, parse that file only ([outbound_one_hop]).
    5. Colour resolvable links. Keep URL and wildcard links. Show an error for an
       unresolved idea. Show an error for an unresolved import ([missing_reference_colour_sequence]).
    6. Show lazy features when they are ready ([lazy_features_after_outbound]).
       They must not block steps 1–5.

    Outbound links must be self-contained: one buffer parse plus one native parse per
    unique neighbor file, with a content-hash cache ([neighbor_parse]).
    The host native extract is cached by URI plus text fingerprint ([open_file_hot_path]).
    If the workspace index can finish in less than one second, inbound pointing still
    waits for SQLite. Outbound pointing must not wait for that index.

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [neighbor_parse]
        [outbound_presentation]
        [local_symbolic_links]
        [document_links]
        [semantic_tokens]
        [document_factory]
        [document_builder]
        [language_server_main]
        [native_parse]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:links a neighbor idea after a depth-1 parse without loading the target document"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:does not link when the neighbor file exists but the idea is missing"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:does not parse a neighbor of the neighbor"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/local-symbolic-links.test.ts:same-file idea links without DocumentBuilder / workspace link"]
    )
}

open_file_sequence_diagram {
    [open_file_algorithm]
    Actors: VS Code editor, TextMate grammar, extension host, VS Code LSP API,
    Langium functions, native extract, file system, SQLite index, lazy extra features.

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant User
        participant Editor as VS Code editor
        participant TextMate as TextMate grammar
        participant ExtHost as Extension host
        participant VscLsp as VS Code LSP API
        participant Langium as Langium functions
        participant Native as Native extract
        participant Fs as File system
        participant Sqlite as SQLite index
        participant Lazy as Lazy extra features

        User->>Editor: Open or change .rq file
        Editor->>TextMate: Tokenise buffer
        TextMate-->>Editor: Immediate syntax colour
        Editor->>ExtHost: didOpen / didChange
        ExtHost->>VscLsp: textDocument/didOpen or didChange
        VscLsp->>Langium: Parse this buffer (factory populate or replace)
        Langium-->>VscLsp: CST and AST on parseResult (Parsed)
        Note over Langium: Linked and Validated do not rebuild this AST
        VscLsp-->>Editor: Semantic tokens from this AST
        VscLsp->>Native: analyzeLocalSymbolic(this file)
        Native-->>VscLsp: Ideas, outbound edges, same-file inbound
        loop each unique neighbor file (depth 1)
            VscLsp->>Fs: Read neighbor text
            VscLsp->>Native: Parse neighbor ideas only
            Native-->>VscLsp: Neighbor idea names and lines
            Note over Langium: Do not populate a Langium AST for the neighbor
        end
        VscLsp-->>Editor: Resolvable links, URL links, wildcard links
        VscLsp-->>Editor: Error for unresolved ideas and imports
        Note over Sqlite,Lazy: Must not block outbound links
        ExtHost->>Sqlite: Soft sync when the index is ready
        Sqlite-->>Lazy: Inbound snapshot, catalogs
        Lazy-->>Editor: Inlay hints, CodeLens, completion
    ```
}

ast_lifecycle {
    The Langium AST is the Chevrotain tree on `document.parseResult`.
    Native [local_symbolic_analysis] is a separate idea list. It is not this AST.
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [open_file_sequence_diagram], [outbound_one_hop],
    [token_colour_sequence], [parse_budget_timeout],
    ["./initialisation-and-sequencing.rq".lsp_file_watch].

    Populate. The document factory parses this buffer when the editor opens it,
    when workspace load first reads that URI, or when a caller uses `fromString`.
    After parse, the document is at `DocumentState.Parsed`. The CST and the AST exist then.
    Semantic tokens and outbound identification may run.

    Replace. When this buffer text changes, the factory parses again and replaces
    `parseResult`. It does not patch the old tree. Then the open-file sequence runs again
    from colour tokens. A watched `.rq` change uses the same replace path
    ([document_update_handler]). If the text is unchanged, keep the current tree.

    Do not rebuild. DocumentBuilder phases after Parsed (`IndexedContent`, `ComputedScopes`,
    `Linked`, `IndexedReferences`, `Validated`) attach scopes, links, and diagnostics.
    They must not replace the AST ([document_builder]).

    Do not populate a Langium AST for a neighbor during [outbound_one_hop].
    A change to a neighbor file does not replace this buffer's AST.
    Outbound confirmation reads neighbor text again (cache by fingerprint).
    Background workspace parse may populate ASTs for other files ([workspace_manager]).
    That work must not gate outbound links. Open buffers parse first.

    Incomplete parse. If the budget fails, the factory stores an empty model plus
    diagnostics ([parse_budget_timeout]). Idea lists on that AST stay empty until a
    later successful parse.

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Editor as VS Code editor
        participant Factory as Document factory
        participant Parser as Langium parser
        participant Builder as DocumentBuilder
        participant Native as Native extract
        participant Neighbor as Neighbor 1-hop

        alt Open this buffer or first workspace load of this URI
            Editor->>Factory: didOpen / getOrCreateDocument
            Factory->>Parser: parse or parseAsync (this text)
            Parser-->>Factory: CST and AST
            Factory-->>Editor: parseResult populated (Parsed)
        else Change this buffer text
            Editor->>Factory: didChange / factory.update
            Factory->>Parser: parseAsync (new text)
            Parser-->>Factory: New CST and AST
            Factory-->>Editor: parseResult replaced (Parsed)
            Note over Factory: Do not patch the old tree
        else Text unchanged
            Factory-->>Editor: Keep current parseResult
        else Parse budget fails
            Parser-->>Factory: Empty model plus diagnostics
            Factory-->>Editor: Incomplete AST (no idea names)
        end
        Builder->>Builder: Index, scopes, link, validate
        Note over Builder: Same AST. Do not rebuild the tree.
        Native-->>Editor: Separate idea list for this file
        Note over Neighbor: Native parse only. No Langium AST for the neighbor.
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [document_factory]
        [async_parser]
        [parse_budget]
        [workspace_manager]
        [document_update_handler]
        [document_builder]
        [neighbor_parse]
        [language_server_main]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:populates the Langium AST at Parsed without DocumentBuilder"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:replaces the AST when this buffer text changes"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:keeps the AST when the text is unchanged"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:linking and validation do not replace the AST"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:neighbor hop does not populate a Langium AST"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:incomplete parse stores an empty model"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/parse-budget.test.ts:times out a hung parse worker with warning and error"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:open-file-sequencing.rq parses mermaid sequence diagrams"]
    )
}

token_colour_sequence {
    Token colour has two layers. They must not wait for SQLite or for workspace Linked.
    TextMate paints first from the buffer text. Semantic tokens paint after the Langium AST
    is populated ([ast_lifecycle]). Native extract does not paint tokens.
    Missing references keep the same token colour. The error underline is a diagnostic,
    not a different semantic token ([missing_reference_colour_sequence], [reference_rendering]).
    Related: [syntax_highlighting].

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Editor as VS Code editor
        participant TextMate as TextMate grammar
        participant VscLsp as VS Code LSP API
        participant Langium as Langium functions
        participant Native as Native extract

        Editor->>TextMate: Buffer text
        TextMate-->>Editor: Scopes for ideas, imports, links, comments
        Editor->>VscLsp: semanticTokens/full (DocumentState.Parsed)
        VscLsp->>Langium: Walk AST
        Langium-->>Editor: Types, namespaces, strings, variables
        Note over Native: Native extract does not paint tokens
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../../packages/language/syntaxes/reqlan.tmLanguage.json"]
        [semantic_tokens]
        [language_server_main]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/textmate-import-highlight.test.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/semantic-tokens-wildcard.test.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:semantic tokens are available from Parsed AST without workspace link"]
    )
}

file_crawl_sequence {
    Workspace crawl is the indexer ([index], [index_sequencing]). It is not the open-file path.
    Native sync walks `.rq` files, then allowlisted code files, and writes SQLite.
    Open-file outbound links must not wait for that walk ([open_file_algorithm]).
    Langium watches `.rq` files only (["./initialisation-and-sequencing.rq".lsp_file_watch]).
    Related: [extension_startup_sequence], [background_startup].

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant ExtHost as Extension host
        participant Native as Native sync
        participant Fs as File system
        participant Sqlite as SQLite index
        participant Langium as Langium LSP
        participant Editor as VS Code editor

        ExtHost->>Native: Soft syncWorkspace (mtime skip)
        Native->>Fs: Walk .rq files then code files
        Native->>Sqlite: Upsert ideas and edges
        Note over Langium,Editor: Open-file 1-hop does not wait for this walk
        Sqlite-->>ExtHost: Index ready
        ExtHost->>Langium: Push inbound snapshot for visible editors
        Langium-->>Editor: Lazy inbound inlay and CodeLens
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/workspace-index.ts"]
        ["../../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        [inbound_sync]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/analytical/test/workspace-index.test.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:links a neighbor idea after a depth-1 parse without loading the target document"]
    )
}

outbound_one_hop {
    Cross-file idea confirmation has depth 1: parse the target file, then stop.
    Do not parse files that the neighbor itself references.
    Do not load the neighbor into `LangiumDocuments` (that starts workspace linking).
    Do not read SQLite for outbound confirmation.
    Prefer the open buffer text when the neighbor is already open and dirty.
    Cache neighbor idea lists by URI plus content hash ([neighbor_parse]).
    Cache this buffer's native extract by URI plus text fingerprint so links and
    diagnostics share one host parse ([open_file_hot_path]).
    Native [local_symbolic_analysis] stays file-local. This hop is the LSP layer on top.
    This hop must not populate a Langium AST for the neighbor ([ast_lifecycle]).
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [non_web_reference_navigation].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [neighbor_parse]
        [local_symbolic_links]
        [native_parse]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:links a neighbor idea after a depth-1 parse without loading the target document"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:does not parse a neighbor of the neighbor"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:reuses a cached neighbor parse for the same content"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:reuses the host native extract for links and diagnostics"]
    )
}

open_file_hot_path {
    Open-file work must stay cheap after the first parse of this buffer.
    Cache this buffer's native extract by URI plus text fingerprint. Document links,
    go-to-definition, and outbound diagnostics must reuse that extract until the text
    or import-root mapping changes ([local_symbolic_links]).
    Look up an open neighbor buffer by URI only. Do not match on file basename
    ([neighbor_parse]).
    When another `.rq` file changes, do not relink every document that still has a
    Langium linker error. Relink this document when the index says it is affected,
    when comment references name that file, or when this document's outbound targets
    include the changed URI ([document_builder]).
    Drop a false unresolved diagnostic only for the overlapping idea-name range.
    Do not drop a different missing name on the same line ([outbound_presentation]).
    At `DocumentState.Parsed`, publish lex/parse diagnostics with outbound idea errors
    so the editor does not wait for Validated to see a broken parse.
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [outbound_one_hop], [ast_lifecycle],
    [comment_backlink_sequence].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [local_symbolic_links]
        [neighbor_parse]
        [document_builder]
        [outbound_presentation]
        [comment_diagnostics]
        ["../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-parse-diagnostics.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:reuses the host native extract for links and diagnostics"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:reparses the host native extract when this buffer text changes"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:does not treat a same-name file as the loaded neighbor"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:does not relink an unrelated file that still has linker errors"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:relinks a host when its neighbor file changes"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/comment-reference-resolution.test.ts:relinks comment references only when the target file changes"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/comment-reference-resolution.test.ts:revalidates comment-reference underlines when a matching idea is created on disk"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:keeps a missing idea error on the same line as a confirmed neighbor idea"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:Parsed outbound publish includes lex parse diagnostics"]
    )
}

missing_reference_colour_sequence {
    After [outbound_one_hop], paint links and errors as follows:
    - URL references: document link, no error.
    - Wildcard references: document link (command target), no error underline for zero matches
      (warning stays on the validator).
    - File or import path missing: error underline, no document link
      ([file_reference_errors], [import_does_not_exist_error]).
    - Neighbor file exists and the named idea exists: document link to that idea line.
    - Neighbor file exists and the named idea is missing: error underline, no document link.
    - Same-file idea missing: error underline, no document link.
    One-hop that confirms an idea must drop a false Langium linking error for that range.
    Do not drop a different missing name that only shares the line.
    Related: [unresolved_reference_diagnostics], [reference_rendering].

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Langium as Langium functions
        participant Native as Native extract
        participant Fs as File system
        participant Editor as VS Code editor

        Langium->>Native: Outbound edges from this file
        alt URL or wildcard
            Langium-->>Editor: Document link (no unresolved error)
        else File or import path missing
            Fs-->>Langium: Not found
            Langium-->>Editor: Error underline, no document link
        else Neighbor exists, idea missing
            Langium->>Native: Parse neighbor (depth 1)
            Native-->>Langium: Idea list without the name
            Langium-->>Editor: Error underline, no document link
        else Neighbor exists, idea present
            Langium->>Native: Parse neighbor (depth 1)
            Native-->>Langium: Idea name and line
            Langium-->>Editor: Document link to idea line
            Note over Langium: Drop false linker unresolved for that range
        else Same-file idea missing
            Langium-->>Editor: Error underline, no document link
        end
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [outbound_presentation]
        [local_symbolic_links]
        [document_links]
        ["../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-validator.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:does not link when the neighbor file exists but the idea is missing"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:keeps URL and wildcard document links"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:drops a false unresolved diagnostic when the neighbor idea exists"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:keeps a missing idea error on the same line as a confirmed neighbor idea"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:reports an unresolved import path"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/local-symbolic-links.test.ts:unresolved same-file ideas get no document link"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/local-symbolic-links.test.ts:missing cross-file targets do not get document links"]
    )
}

comment_backlink_sequence {
    `rq:[idea]` and `rq:["path".idea]` in code comments use the same depth-1 confirmation.
    Qualified path: read that `.rq` file, parse idea names, then link or error.
    Unqualified name: search open `.rq` buffers first; SQLite may fill later ([lazy_features_after_outbound]).
    Do not create a happy document link when the idea is not confirmed.
    Related: [comment_reference_resolution_error_state].

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Editor as VS Code editor
        participant ExtHost as Extension host
        participant Langium as Langium functions
        participant Native as Native extract
        participant Fs as File system
        participant Sqlite as SQLite index

        Editor->>ExtHost: Open code file with rq comment
        ExtHost->>ExtHost: Find rq tokens in comments
        alt Qualified path
            ExtHost->>Fs: Read target .rq (depth 1)
            ExtHost->>Native: Parse idea names
            alt Idea declared
                Native-->>Editor: Document link
            else Idea or file missing
                Native-->>Editor: Error underline, no link
            end
        else Unqualified name
            ExtHost->>ExtHost: Search open .rq buffers
            opt Index ready
                Sqlite-->>ExtHost: Optional later match
            end
        end
        Note over Langium: .rq files use the same 1-hop helper
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [comment_diagnostics]
        [comment_links_host]
        [neighbor_parse]
        ["../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-comment-resolver.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:comment references confirm the neighbor idea without loading Langium"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/comment-reference-resolution.test.ts:reports a missing comment reference idea in a loaded file"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/comment-reference-resolution.test.ts:shares one presentation so a matching idea clears the underline and adds a link"]
    )
}

lazy_features_after_outbound {
    After outbound links and errors are on screen, show extra features when their data is ready:
    - SQLite inbound snapshot ([unify_inbound_indexes]) for inlay hints ([inlay_hints])
    - Reference CodeLens ([codelens])
    - Attribute and name catalogs for completion and quick fixes
    - Activity-bar local symbolic merge
    These features must not delay [open_file_algorithm] steps 1–5.
    Related: [language_server], [background_startup].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [inbound_sync]
        ["../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-inlay-hint-provider.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-code-lens-provider.ts"]
        ["../../../packages/extension/src/extension/main.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../packages/language/test/inbound-referencer-index-perf.test.ts:inlay referencers come from the pushed snapshot, not findAllReferences"]
        ["../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:links a neighbor idea after a depth-1 parse without loading the target document"]
    )
}
